OL,3,GNEWSA'Unreasonable delay' in spotting
OL,4,Acancer in patient who later died
OL,5,
OL,6,FA patient's concerns that they had
OL,7,Fcancer were not followed up immediately
OL,8,Fby their doctor, a health watchdog has
OL,9,Fsaid.
OL,11,FThe patient was diagnosed with diabetes
OL,12,Fafter experiencing unexplained weight
OL,13,Floss, but after their symptoms
OL,14,Fcontinued over the following months
OL,15,Fthey asked the GP if it might be
OL,16,Fpancreatic cancer.
OL,18,FThe patient was referred to specialists
OL,19,Fin stomach disorders before blood tests
OL,20,Fled to pancreatic cancer being
OL,21,Fdiagnosed. The patient died about six
OL,22,Fweeks later.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,430,420,260,160,0,100
